 second equation, we get a false statement $0=-1.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$" 13194139542404 17592186576411 false] [17592186120516 1071 "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" 13194139542404 17592186576411 true] [17592186120516 1071 "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" 13194139542404 17592186576411 false] [17592186120516 1074 "We know that $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Span}\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}},{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}} & =\\mathbf{b} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2} &=-12 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2} &=-10 \\\\ -6{x}_{1}+18{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-3 & 9 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+24\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+24.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+24\\,⇒\\,k=-24.\n$$" 13194139542404 17592186576411 true] [17592186120516 1074 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2} &=-12 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2} &=-10 \\\\ -6{x}_{1}+18{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-3 & 9 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+24\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+24.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+24\\,⇒\\,k=-24.\n$$" 13194139542404 17592186576411 false] [17592186120525 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{{\\mathbf{b}}_{1},{\\mathbf{b}}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n