[17592186481356 1074 "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[A\\,|\\,b] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k+30\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 12 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k+30\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 21 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k+30\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k+30\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=12 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=7 \\\\ 0 &=k-5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-5,$ which means that $k=5.$" 13194139542404 17592186576411 true] [17592186481379 1074 "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ then the equation $Cx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & k-4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ -4{x}_{2} &=6 \\\\ 0 &=k-1.\\end{aligned}\\r